From 817b75b6b093f1a22b93151d358d3b4d384e9649 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: y700 workspace <304558835+bobsixsixsix-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: disable SDI when download mode is
 switched off

qcom_scm_probe() disables the Secure Debug Image (SDI) only when
download mode is already off at probe time, or when the device tree
marks it as enabled by default (qcom,sdi-enabled). Switching download
mode off later, through the download_mode module parameter, only clears
the download mode bits in TCSR. SDI stays armed: a watchdog bite or
another reset that the firmware handles still enters the debug image,
and the device waits in the dump mode screen instead of rebooting.

Disable SDI as well when download mode is set to "off" after probe, and
log the result of the SCM call. Setting it back to "full" or "mini"
does not re-enable SDI; that takes a reboot.

y700 (kernel y16): written here, not taken from upstream. On 2026-10-31
msm_mdss_irq() took a synchronous external abort reading the
MDSS interrupt status register. CPU0 stopped in the middle of the oops,
panic() never ran, and the firmware reset the tablet into dump mode,
where it stayed until it was forced off. download_mode
had been "off" since three minutes after boot (y700-dumpmode-off
service). The kernel command line still sets
qcom_scm.download_mode=full (CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE), so probe leaves SDI
armed and the first minutes after boot keep their dumps; with this
change SDI is disabled when the service switches download mode off.
The log line is "download mode off, SDI disable: <result>".

y700 patch file: 1058-firmware-qcom-scm-disable-SDI-when-download-mode-is-switched-off.patch

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 3eaa4c9..8a4d5e9 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2735,8 +2735,18 @@ static int set_download_mode(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
 	download_mode = ret;
 	/* Pairs with smp_store_release() in qcom_scm_probe(). */
 	scm = smp_load_acquire(&__scm);
-	if (scm)
+	if (scm) {
 		qcom_scm_set_download_mode(scm, download_mode);
+		/*
+		 * Probe disables SDI only when download mode is already off;
+		 * switched off later, a watchdog bite would still end in the
+		 * debug image and wait in dump mode.
+		 */
+		if (download_mode == QCOM_DLOAD_NODUMP) {
+			ret = qcom_scm_disable_sdi();
+			dev_info(scm->dev, "download mode off, SDI disable: %d\n", ret);
+		}
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
